// A walkthrough is a narrated tour for presenting to a room. Its steps show views (optionally
// focused on some elements) or play a scenario, whole or a range of its steps. A step can open
// or close containers and switch the audience. Narration can be reworded per audience.

model library: Town library

borrower: Borrower [person]

library: Library system | Lends books [system]
  catalogue: Catalogue | Every book and where it is [service]
    search: Search | Finds books by title or author [module]
    holds: Holds | Keeps books for borrowers [module]
  loans: Loans | Who has which book [service]
  loans-db: Loans database | Every loan [store]

borrower finds books with search
borrower places holds with holds
holds checks availability with loans
loans saves loans in loans-db

view big-picture: Big picture
  show borrower, library +1

scenario hold: Placing a hold
  borrower places a hold with holds
  holds checks availability with loans
  loans returns the answer to holds
  holds confirms the hold to borrower

walkthrough tour: A tour of the library system
  step big-picture
    > Borrowers use one system, which has three parts.
  step big-picture: catalogue
    > The **Catalogue** is what borrowers see.
    @exec > The **Catalogue** is where borrowers find and reserve books.
  step big-picture: holds
    open catalogue
    > Inside it, **Holds** keeps books aside for borrowers.
  step hold: 1-2
    > A hold starts with a check that the book is free.
  step hold: 3-4
    for engineer
    > Then the answer comes back and the borrower hears about it.
    @engineer >> The check is a synchronous call; nothing is queued.
